%erg v1
Title: Fix test_ready.sh hygiene: stale comment and fragile JSON extraction
Created: 2026-05-05
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-05-05T08:34Z claude created

--- body ---
Two hygiene issues in `tests/test_ready.sh`:

**1. Stale comment at line 290:**
```sh
# --- Empty dir ---
```
This comment precedes the forge-ref blocker test, not the empty-dir test. The
actual empty-dir test begins at line 312 with its own `# --- Empty dir handled ---`
comment. Delete the stale label at line 290.

**2. Fragile JSON extraction at line ~380:**
```sh
entry=$(echo "$output" | tr '\n' ' ' | grep -o '{[^}]*"id": "0098"[^}]*}')
```
The `[^}]` character class breaks if the 0098 entry has a nested object (e.g.,
a `blocked_by` array like `[{"kind": "local", "id": "0042"}]`). The current
0098 fixture has no blockers so it works, but any future blocker addition
silently breaks the match.

**Fix:** Replace with grep for individual fields on the collapsed JSON:
```sh
if echo "$output" | tr -d '\n' | grep -q '"id": "0098"'; then ...
if echo "$output" | tr -d '\n' | grep -q '"claimed": true'; then ...
```
Do not rely on `{[^}]*}` matching a nested JSON structure.
